cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "pyperformance: The Python Performance Benchmark Suite"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The pyperformance contributors"
url: "https://github.com/python/pyperformance"
repository-code: "https://github.com/python/pyperformance"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  The pyperformance project is intended to be an authoritative source of
  benchmarks for all Python implementations. The focus is on real-world
  benchmarks, rather than synthetic benchmarks, using whole applications
  when possible.
keywords:
  - Python
  - benchmark
  - performance
